 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "can · could · must · have to",
   "en": "can · could · must · have to"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "can은 능력과 허락, could는 과거의 능력을 나타냅니다. must와 have to는 '~해야 한다'이고, 부정은 뜻이 다릅니다. mustn't는 '하면 안 된다(금지)', don't have to는 '할 필요가 없다'입니다. 조동사 뒤에는 동사 원형을 씁니다.",
   "en": "Can shows ability and permission; could shows past ability. Must and have to mean 'it is necessary', but their negatives are different: mustn't means 'it is forbidden' and don't have to means 'it is not necessary'. After a modal use the base verb."
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "표현 / Form",
    "뜻 / Meaning",
    "예문 / Example"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "can / can't",
     "능력·허락 / ability, permission",
     "I can swim."
    ],
    [
     "could",
     "과거 능력 / past ability",
     "I could swim at five."
    ],
    [
     "must / have to",
     "의무 / necessary",
     "You must wear a cap."
    ],
    [
     "mustn't",
     "금지 / forbidden",
     "You mustn't run."
    ],
    [
     "don't have to",
     "불필요 / not necessary",
     "You don't have to pay."
    ]
   ]
  },
  "notes": [
   {
    "ko": "조동사에는 -s가 붙지 않습니다: He can swim (✕ He cans).",
    "en": "Modals take no -s: He can swim (not He cans)."
   },
   {
    "ko": "mustn't와 don't have to는 뜻이 완전히 다릅니다.",
    "en": "Mustn't and don't have to mean very different things."
   },
   {
    "ko": "have to는 주어에 따라 has to가 됩니다: She has to work.",
    "en": "'Have to' becomes has to with he / she / it: She has to work."
   }
  ],
  "examples": [
